{
  "name": "Mutation",
  "icon": "hexalia:mutavis",
  "category": "hexalia:core_mechanics",
  "sortnum": 4,
  "pages": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Mutation",
      "text": "Mutavis awakens hidden possibilities in compatible blocks. Use it on a block and wait a short time for the transformation."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Using Mutavis",
      "anchor": "usage",
      "text": "Grind Tree Resin, a Slimeball, and any crushed herb in the $(l:hexalia:core_mechanics/mortar_and_pestle)Mortar and Pestle$(/l). Hold the resulting Mutavis and use it on a block shown in the recipes below."
    },
    {
      "type": "hexalia:recipe_page",
      "recipe_id": "hexalia:mutavis_from_mortar",
      "layout": "mortar_and_pestle"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Area Mutation",
      "anchor": "area",
      "text": "Using Mutavis on a $(l:hexalia:core_mechanics/enchanted_plants#morphora)Morphora$(/l) spreads mutation to nearby compatible blocks. Each successful transformation uses nearby Grass, leaving Coarse Dirt; failures leave the Grass untouched."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "On Results",
      "anchor": "results",
      "text": "Mutations may either replace the original block or produce their result as an item. This behavior can be configured, allowing different approaches to resource gathering."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Automation",
      "anchor": "automation",
      "text": "Mutavis can be applied using dispensers, enabling automated mutation of blocks or Morphora flowers when supplied with the necessary resources."
    },
